"[2605.02273] These Aren't the Reviews You're Looking For How Humans Review AI-Generated Pull Requests (https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02273)\nciteturn15view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02273\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Software Engineering\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 4 May 2026]\nL9: # Title:These Aren't the Reviews You're Looking For How Humans Review AI-Generated Pull Requests\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Kacper Duma (1), cite6†Patryk Wróblewski (1), cite7†Jagoda Bobińska (1), cite8†Julia Winiarska (1), cite9†Piotr Przymus (1) ((1) Nicolaus Copernicus University in Toruń, Toruń, Poland)\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled These Aren't the Reviews You're Looking For How Humans Review AI-Generated Pull Requests, by Kacper Duma (1) and 6 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite10†View PDF cite11†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We analyze code review interactions for AI-generated pull requests (PRs) on GitHub using the AIDev dataset and compare them to human-authored PRs within the same repositories. We find that most AI-generated PRs receive no review and, when reviewed, are largely dominated by AI agents rather than humans. Human-authored PRs are more likely to receive human-only review and to attract direct human feedback.\nL17: In contrast, reviews of AI-generated PRs more often take the form of automation-mediated interaction, with human involvement frequently expressed through agent steering rather than standalone evaluation. These results indicate systematic differences in how review activity is structured in agentic workflows and raise challenges for interpreting review metrics as indicators of human oversight in large-scale mining studies.\nL18: Comments:  | Accepted to EASE 2026\nL19: Subjects:  | Software Engineering (cs.SE)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite12†arXiv:2605.02273 [cs.SE]\nL21:    | (or cite13†arXiv:2605.02273v1 [cs.SE] for this version)\nL22:    | cite14†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2605.02273†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Piotr Przymus [cite15†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Mon, 4 May 2026 06:32:50 UTC (54 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled These Aren't the Reviews You're Looking For How Humans Review AI-Generated Pull Requests, by Kacper Duma (1) and 6 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * cite10†View PDF L35:   * cite11†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite16†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite17†view license†creativecommons.org L39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: cs.SE\nL42: \nL43: cite18†< prev |   cite19†next > L44: \nL45: cite20†new | cite21†recent | cite22†2026-05 L46: \nL47: Change to browse by:\nL48: \nL49: cite23†cs L50: \nL51: ### References & Citations\nL52: \nL53:   * cite24†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L54:   * cite25†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L55:   * cite26†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L56: \nL57: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL58: \nL59: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL60: \nL61: [Button: ×]\nL62: \nL63: loading...\nL64: \nL65: Data provided by:\nL66: \nL67: ### Bookmark\nL68: \nL69: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL70: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL71: \nL72: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL73: \nL74: Bibliographic Explorer (cite27†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL75: \nL76: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL77: \nL78: Connected Papers (cite28†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com )\nL79: \nL80: [Input] Litmaps Toggle\nL81: \nL82: Litmaps (cite29†What is Litmaps?†www.litmaps.co